sts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EGAMatsu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EGAMatsu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EGAMatsu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EGAMatsu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EGAMatsu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EGAMatsu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EGAMatsu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-15T08:53:46Z","updated_at":"2026-02-15T09:13:56Z","body":"I find it funny how long this PR has taken, given how it's 1 line of code (and it's just a variable in an array), and given it's been SO long that the EDITOR got the language before projects could even properly list the language/select from it.\r\n\r\nIt feels backwards that the EDITOR got support for the language, before the RUNTIME got proper support.\r\nI get the whole \"custom locale\" thing, but that shouldn't even be needed, ESPECIALLY if the Editor already can properly be USED in the language.\r\n\r\nIt's just pretty silly, and given it's been about A YEAR since I opened this; it's even more silly, given the reason was for a feature that isn't even close to being worked on.\r\n\r\nI hope I don't sound like, rude or anything, but I just find this all silly; I just think the language should've been properly labeled for months, given the whole fact that you can select the language as the editors language.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3903803569/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3910532702","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/102787#issuecomment-3910532